{"duration_api_ms":92930,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"57267af8-3660-4a8e-8315-fc4981a09f64","total_cost_usd":0.6059122,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37205,"cache_read_input_tokens":633621,"output_tokens":9073,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37205,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1043,"cache_read_input_tokens":68209,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1334},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":9073,"cacheReadInputTokens":633621,"cacheCreationInputTokens":37205,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6059122,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":164,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":37205,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":11,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've written the test plan for porting upstream fix 81576 (`.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-81576-test-plan.md`) and committed it as `9a0fc4b`. The plan comes from reading the upstream patch and EO's current code. I didn't run any code or tests, and I left the full end-to-end check for the port itself. The acceptance command passes, `theseus scope-check` is clean, and `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 4 warnings.\n\n**How the bug works today:** when the final save of a document fails, the code puts its database entry back into the \"saving\" state (`SaveVersion`) and nothing ever moves it out again. Shutdown waits until no document is in that state, so it runs until its timeout and reports failure. Retries are turned off during shutdown, so a failed save while shutting down always leaves a stuck entry.\n\n**What the fix changes:**\n- **Stuck state:** a failed save with no retry left now marks the document as openable, with a \"file not assembled\" flag, instead of leaving it in `SaveVersion`. Shutdown can then finish.\n- **Unsaved edits:** these are kept, and the editor shows a \"File not assembled\" warning on every open until a later save clears the flag.\n- **What counts as success:** an acknowledgement from the integrator only counts as a successful save if the save worked, or if the error was the \"corrupted file\" one.\n\n**Something PKT-0029 missed:** on EO main today, if the save fails for a reason other than a corrupted file (for example a converter crash) and the integrator still acknowledges the \"Corrupted\" callback, EO treats it as a success and deletes the unsaved edits. So the fix also closes a data-loss path, not only the shutdown hang.\n\n**Test plan:** the tests are meant to be written first against EO main, so they record how it behaves today. They cover the save callback (T1–T9), the editor warning on open (E1–E5), the shutdown wait (S1–S2) and the new helper file. After the port, only four of them should change result (T3, T4, T6, E2). The plan also covers the end-to-end check using the running document server and browser, and the one conflict to fix by hand when applying the patch.\n\n**Recommendation for the human decision:** port it, with the characterization tests written first in a separate packet. The reason to wait instead is that the fix exists only on upstream `master` (no release branch) and adds a new database state integrators may notice. One gap remains either way: a corrupted-file error with no acknowledgement and no retry still leaves the stuck state (T9).\n\n**Follow-up:** I recorded a request for the characterization-tests packet in `.theseus/spawn/`. It only creates files under `tests/unit` and changes no source code.\n\n**Lesson for the Atlas:** in docservice, the save callback treats any acknowledgement as success, even when the save failed for a reason other than a corrupted file. Shutdown counts documents still in `SaveVersion`, so any path that restores that state without a retry can hang shutdown.\n\nThe Executor log, Lessons section and friction line are filled in. The friction line notes that `theseus packet new` refused `--type test`; the executor prompt doesn't list the valid types.","ttft_ms":3080,"type":"result","duration_ms":108909,"uuid":"49b11ab8-9345-4d28-b7bd-1883ebfe3894","ttft_stream_ms":1830,"time_to_request_ms":422,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":232,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":16,"input_attachments":56,"input_hooks":5,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":33,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":9,"auto_mode_context_wait":12,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":16,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":62,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":194,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":209,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":137,"process_rss_mib_result":219,"process_anon_mib_result":130,"process_peak_rss_mib":234,"process_cpu_ms_turn":2428,"process_wall_ms_turn":108908,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1090,"process_wall_ms_streaming":70442,"main_stream_count":11,"main_stream_event_c